		"Fuel mode:  A = sender only: JP1 1-2, fit JP2.   B = gauge + dash: JP1 2-3, JP2 off.\nOil + tach: +12V -> 2.2k -> yellow status LED -> PC817 LED -> sensor wire. Switch closes to chassis = LED on = GPIO low.\nFilter + temp (monitored): fit a 4.7k resistor across each switch AT THE SWITCH. Wire reads ~1.65 V OK, ~0 V switch closed,\n3.3 V wire broken (NO SIGNAL). Their LEDs are driven by the Pi.\nF1: 5 A (Pi 4 or Pi 5).  D1 (TVS) clamps spikes and blows F1 if power is connected backwards.\nPower hold: +12V_IN is the CONSTANT battery feed. Q2 switches it to +12V while the key is on (IGN) or the Pi holds HOLD\n(GPIO26) high. At the end of shutdown the Pi raises KILL (GPIO16): Q4 cuts power. U6 cuts power ~3 min after key-off if\nthe Pi never does. Key-off draw with everything off: under 0.1 mA.\nLights: sense wires from the LAMP side of each light switch (inline 1 A fuse at the tap). Light on = yellow LED on = GPIO low.\nTach: J12 COIL = ignition coil NEGATIVE terminal (spikes to ~400 V): R80+R81 -> 15 V zener + 1 uF -> PC817 U10.\nU10 and U4 (Hall) share TACH_GPIO: connect the coil OR a Hall sensor, not both. 4-cyl coil: pulses_per_rev = 2.\nLabels with the same name are connected (flag-shaped = between blocks). GND / +3V3 / +5V at the Pi header and modules\nare the same supplies as the ground and supply symbols."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 434.34 157.48 0)
